SCOPE OF THIS LICENCE (not part of the MIT terms above)

This licence covers the ClaimSense source code, tests, configuration files,
notebooks and documentation written for this project, and the trained LoRA
adapter weights, calibrator and threshold files in models/.

It does NOT cover, and grants no rights in:

  1. Ombudsman decisions, awards or any text derived from them, including the
     processed dataset and the precedent index. These remain subject to the
     terms of their publishers:
       - Council for Insurance Ombudsmen (India), cioins.co.in
       - Financial Ombudsman Service (UK), financial-ombudsman.org.uk
       - Financial Services and Pensions Ombudsman (Ireland), fspo.ie
     See DATA_SOURCES.md and docs/data/terms-of-use-audit.md for what may be
     used and published for each source, and the required attribution.

  2. Third-party base models downloaded at run time (for example
     answerdotai/ModernBERT-base, BAAI/bge-small-en-v1.5,
     cross-encoder/nli-deberta-v3-base). Each is governed by the licence on its
     own model card.

  3. Third-party Python packages, which are governed by their own licences.

ClaimSense describes how similar past cases were decided. It is not legal
advice; the ombudsman decides each case on its own facts.
